# Catalog: products, tags, utensils (API.md §2). Sign in first with dev-login (Development only).
# For admin calls sign in with an email listed in Admin__Emails__0. Task B2 uses database recipes_b2.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5102/api/v1
@productId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@targetId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Sign in (dev-login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "email": "anna@test.local", "nickname": "anna" }

### Search products (prefix first, then trigram similarity)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?q=smiet&limit=10

### Products by category
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?category=dairy

### Get a product
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}

### Add a product (409 product.duplicate carries existingId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "name": "Czosnek niedźwiedzi", "category": "vegetables", "measureKind": "count", "displayClass": "piece", "hasSizes": true, "allowHalf": true, "gramsPerPiece": 40 }

### Edit a product (admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "name": "Cebula", "category": "vegetables", "measureKind": "count", "displayClass": "piece", "hasSizes": true, "allowHalf": true }

### Merge a product into another (admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}/merge
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "targetId": "{{targetId}}" }

### Tags
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags?q=sniad

### Create a tag (200 with the existing tag on a normalized match; "szybkie" is reserved)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "name": "na imprezę" }

### Utensils
GET {{baseUrl}}/utensils?q=blen

### Create a utensil
POST {{baseUrl}}/utensils
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "name": "Blender" }
